    Question: Philip has a farm with animals. He has 20 cows, 50% more ducks. Philip also has as many pigs as one-fifth of ducks and cows in total. How many animals does Philip have on his farm? Think step by step. Answer:Philip has 20 cows. He has 50% more ducks, so he has 20 * 50% = 10 more ducks. He now has 20 + 10 = 30 ducks. He also has as many pigs as one-fifth of ducks and cows in total. One-fifth of ducks and cows is 1/5 * (30 + 20) = 1/5 * 50 = 10. So Philip has 10 pigs. In total, Philip has 20 + 30 + 10 = 60 animals on his farm. #### 60 The answer is: 60

